{"entry_id": 1166, "lemma": "δαιμονιώδης", "page": 65, "text": "δαιμονιώδης, demon-like, such as demons have.", "gloss": "demon-like, such as demons have", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1167, "lemma": "δαίμων", "page": 65, "text": "δαίμων, an evil-spirit, a demon, much less common than the diminutive δαιμόνιον.", "gloss": "an evil-spirit, a demon", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1168, "lemma": "δάκνω", "page": 65, "text": "δάκνω, I bite; hence, I backbite, or harm seriously.", "gloss": "I bite", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1170, "lemma": "δακρύω", "page": 65, "text": "δακρύω, I shed tears, weep.", "gloss": "I shed tears, weep", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1171, "lemma": "δακτύλιος", "page": 65, "text": "δακτύλιος, a finger-ring.", "gloss": "a finger-ring", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1172, "lemma": "δάκτυλος", "page": 65, "text": "δάκτυλος, a finger: the picturesque δακτύλῳ of Lk. xi 20 is represented by πνεύματι in Mt. xii 28.", "gloss": "a finger", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1173, "lemma": "Δαλμανουθά", "page": 65, "text": "Δαλμανουθά, Dalmanutha: nothing is known of name or place, and text is probably corrupt (a conjecture of Burkitt in Amer. Journ. Theol. xv (1911) 174).", "gloss": "Dalmanutha", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1174, "lemma": "Δαλματία", "page": 65, "text": "Δαλματία, Dalmatia, a province of the Roman Empire, E. of the Adriatic, a later name for part of what was earlier called Illyricum (Rom. xv 19).", "gloss": "Dalmatia, a province of the Roman Empire", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
{"entry_id": 1175, "lemma": "δαμάζω", "page": 65, "text": "δαμάζω, I tame, subdue, involving obedience and restraint.", "gloss": "I tame, subdue", "status": "ok", "note": ""}
